NOTE  What IS documented, from sources that are in the corpus:
NOTE    - US 577,329 states on its own face: "Patented in Germany October 11, 1890, No. 57,417, and in England October 13, 1890, No. 16,279."
NOTE    - Google Patents' xhr/query endpoint (a public JSON endpoint, not blocked) returns
NOTE      DE57417C  title "Process for compacting metal castings by means of electricity", assignee "N. SLAwianoff in St. Petersburg, Grofse Morskaia Str. 15"
NOTE      DE65892C  title "Method and device for melting by means of electricity",        assignee "N. SLAWIANOFF in St. Petersburg, Grofse Morskaiastr. 15"
NOTE    - Stahl und Eisen 1892 carries the German filing notice (in the corpus, two scans).
NOTE  These are recorded as EVIDENCE OF EXISTENCE ONLY. No text of DE 57417, DE 65892 or GB 16279 is in this corpus.

# ── the Russian privilege scan ──
FAIL prlib-837493  https://www.prlib.ru/item/837493  page fetched OK; the record reads "Доступно только в Электронных читальных залах" (electronic-reading-room only). ACCESS CONTROL RESPECTED, NOT BYPASSED.
NOTE  Its catalogue record is still useful and is quoted here verbatim: "Привилегия, выданная из Департамента Торговли и Мануфактур в 1891 г. горному инженеру надворному советнику Николаю Славянову, на способ и аппараты для электрической отливки металлов : № 4694/87 : Заявл. 17.03.1890 : Выдача привилегии 13.08.1891 / Николай Славянов. - Санкт-Петербург : Тип. эксп. загот. гос. бумаг, 1891. - 9 с., 1 л. черт. ... Место хранения оригинала: ФИПС"
NOTE  The privilege TEXT that IS in the corpus (privilegiya-1891-otlivka-metallov) comes from the Perm transcription, not from this scan; the filing date 17 March 1890 agrees between the two.

# ── the 1892 first printing ──
FAIL 1892-first-printing  no accessible scan found.  Searched: archive.org metadata (97 «Электричество» items, 30 «Горный журнал» items, language:rus 1885–1902), prlib.ru, search.rsl.ru, elib.shpl.ru, vivaldi.nlr.ru, elib.uraic.ru, elib.biblioatom.ru, geokniga.org, Google Books API.
NOTE  What was reached instead is the Perm transcription of the Машгиз (Moscow, 1954) re-setting, chapters I–IV. Orthography is modernised. Verbatim quotation therefore traces to the 1954 edition, NOT to the 1892 print. Flagged in every affected ledger row.
FAIL weld.pfo-perm.ru (live)  http://weld.pfo-perm.ru/Date/Otlivka1.htm  HTTP 301 -> https://weld.pfo-perm.ru:443/... whose certificate does not match the host name. Certificate verification NOT disabled; the Wayback Machine capture of 2004-05-11 was used instead and is what every URL in the ledger points to.

