# ── deliberately NOT ingested: still in copyright ──
SKIP-COPYRIGHT  Otlivka5.htm / Otlivka6.htm  — К. К. Хренов, С. Т. Назаров, «Биография Н. Г. Славянова» and «Комментарии к книге Н. Г. Славянова», Москва 1954. Khrenov died 1984; the editorial apparatus of the 1954 Mashgiz edition is not public domain. Fetched to read (that is how the copy-text of Otlivka1–4 was identified), NOT written into the corpus.
SKIP-COPYRIGHT  Slavjanov1–4.htm  — А. К. Шарц, «Николай Гаврилович Славянов», Пермь 1965. In copyright.
SKIP-COPYRIGHT  Ubiley.htm  — Р. А. Мусин (ПермГТУ), 2004. In copyright.
SKIP-COPYRIGHT  Malukov.htm  — biography of A. F. Malyukov, 2004, and irrelevant to this person.
NOTE  Consequence to be honest about: the `timeline` lane loses its best material (a full biography) to copyright, exactly as happened with #113 Henderson.

# ── scope of the sweeps that produced the corpus ──
SWEEP  archive.org metadata search built 1341 Latin-script candidate volumes (welding / Stahl und Eisen / ETZ / ZVDI / Dingler / Scientific American Suppl. / Franklin Inst. / AIEE / Iron Age / Electrical World / Electrician). Each was queried through its own item's /fulltext/inside.php for "Benardos", "Slavianoff", "Slawianoff". 58 items came back positive; 36 of those actually contain a Slavianoff spelling in the downloaded DjVuTXT.
SWEEP  A second pool of 326 Russian-language items (97 «Электричество», 30 «Горный журнал», plus language:rus 1885–1902) was downloaded as DjVuTXT and grepped locally for Славянов / Бенардос / «электрическая отливка» in pre-1918 orthography. Only the 1890–1893 «Электричество» run produced hits; «Горный журнал» on archive.org stops at 1882 and contains nothing.
SWEEP  Google Patents' public xhr/query endpoint was searched for slavianoff / slawianoff / slavjanoff / slawjanoff / slavianov / slavyanov / benardos / olszewski / elektrogefest before it began returning 503.

