TIER  P1 8 / S1 22 / S2 23 = 53 files.  Primary share 8/53 = 15.1%, far under the
      70% target and under the 65% floor.  The reason is structural, not effort:
      Slavyanov left a small published body (one book, two Russian privileges, a
      handful of foreign patents, one recorded address), the 1892 first printing is
      not digitised anywhere reachable, and three of his foreign patents are behind
      bot-checks.  The corpus is honest about this rather than promoting S1 to P1.
COUNT 53 files, target ≥50 / floor 45 — MEETS on count.
